ted.\n\n**`internal/knowledge/query.go`** (new)\n- `Count(ctx) (int, error)` → `SELECT COUNT(*)`, no JSON decode.\n- `KnowledgeListQuery{Type, Status, ValidityState, Repository, Source string; Limit int; Cursor string}` and `ListRecords(ctx, q) (records, nextCursor, err)`. SQL WHERE filtering on indexed `type/status/validity_state` and JSON paths `$.scope.repository` / `$.source.provider` (via `JSON_UNQUOTE(JSON_EXTRACT(...))`) happens before decoding. Empty fields = no filter, using the `(? = '' OR col = ?)` pattern. `ORDER BY updated_at DESC, id ASC` with keyset/cursor pagination (`LIMIT Limit+1` to compute `nextCursor`; cursor is base64 of `updated_at|id`). Confirmed the JSON shape against `protocol.KnowledgeRecord` (scope.repository is `*string`; source.provider is a required string).\n\n**`internal/panel/sources/knowledge_source.go`** (rewired `List`)\n- Replaced `AllWithUpdatedAt` + full in-Go filtering with `ListRecords`. Maps `contract.KnowledgeFilter` → `KnowledgeListQuery`. `State`/`Stale` both resolve to `validity_state` (Stale forces \"stale\"; conflicting State+Stale returns empty, matching old behavior). `HasRelation`/`HasConflict` have no SQL column, so they remain a documented post-filter on each returned page; when either is set, `List` seeks through pages until `Limit` post-filtered matches are collected or the store is exhausted, preserving the old \"limit counts post-filtered results\" semantics. Removed the now-unused `matchesKnowledgeFilter`, added `matchesKnowledgePostFilter`.\n\n**`internal/knowledge/query_test.go`** (new) — `TestCount`, `TestListRecordsFiltering` (type/state/repository/source + unmatched), `TestListRecordsCursorPagination` (no dupes, full coverage, terminating cursor, page-size cap), `TestListRecordsRejectsBadCursor`. Reuses the existing `newTestStore` helper.\n\n**`internal/panel/api/knowledge_handler.go`** — not modified. The handler already maps every filter field including `Limit`, and exposing a cursor param would requi