r App.\n- `cmd/punakawan/approvals_cmd.go:51` and `:122`; other cmd files call `loadApp()`.\n\n**`app.Load` (test):** `internal/panel/server/server_test.go:97`; `internal/panel/sources/sources_test.go:78`; `internal/mcpserver/tools_adapters_test.go:58`; `internal/mcpserver/server_test.go:46`; `cmd/punakawan/knowledge_cmd_test.go:22`; `cmd/punakawan/main_test.go:166` and `:223`.\n\n**Per-request panel `Load`/`Close` paths (the Phase 3 target):** `workspace_source.go:120/139` and `global_search_source.go:69`. Note `workspace_source.go` header comment (22-28) explicitly says \"there is no cache yet (a later phase's job)\"; `Get`/`List`→`summaryFor` load-and-close a fresh App per non-primary workspace, each opening a Dolt store via `describe`→`OpenKnowledge` (181).\n\n**Existing partial mitigation:** `internal/panel/sources/cached_workspace.go` — `CachedWorkspaceReader` (wired in `internal/panel/deps.go:48`) fronts `WorkspaceSource` with a stale-while-revalidate `snapshot.Cache` so `/workspaces`, `/overview`, and the reconciler serve cached counts instead of re-running `Load`+Dolt per request. It caches the *snapshot output*, not the `*app.App` itself. `Get` (health page) still delegates to inner `WorkspaceSource.Get` → `app.Load` (cached_workspace.go:101). Global search is not cached.\n\n### 3. `OpenKnowledge` / `OpenSearchIndex` — lazy, memoized\n\n`internal/app/app.go`:\n- **`OpenKnowledge()`** (178-200): checks `isClosed`, locks `knowledgeMu`, returns memoized `a.knowledgeStore` if non-nil (185-187); else re-checks closed under lock, calls `knowledge.Open(a.Supervisor, &lt;root&gt;/.punakawan/knowledge)` (194) — starts/reuses the external Dolt sql-server — and stores it (198). **Cached on the App**, opened once.\n- **`OpenSearchIndex()`** (226-245): same pattern under `searchIndexMu`; returns memoized `a.searchIndex` else `search.OpenIndex(&lt;root&gt;/.punakawan/index/bm25)` (239) and stores (243). **Cached on the App.**\n- `JiraWorkflow()` (206-219): same memoization under `jiraWorkflowMu`.\n- `SearchKnowledge(store, ix, req)` (254-262): holds `searchIndexMu` across `search.Rebuild`+`search.Search`.\n\nSo within one App instance, Dolt/Bleve are opened once and reused; the per-request cost comes from **`Load`+`Close` creating a new App each time** (new Dolt open via `describe`→`OpenKnowledge`), not from reopening within an App.\n\n### 4. Concurrency safety of `*app.App`\n\nPartially safe. The lazy openers are mutex-guarded and safe for concurrent use: `OpenKnowledge`/`OpenSearchIndex`/`JiraWorkflow`/`SearchKnowledge`/`Close` all coordinate via `knowledgeMu`, `searchIndexMu`, `jiraWorkflowMu`, `closedMu` (app.go:45-62, 178-303). The `closed` flag + re-check-under-lock pattern (188-193, 236-238) exists specifically to stop a racing lazy-open from starting an untracked Dolt server after `Close` (comment 51-59). `WorkspaceSource.List` already invokes `describe` (hence `OpenKnowledge`) across a bounded pool of 4 goroutines on the same App (workspace_source.go:90-103), relying on this.\n\nThe other embedded stores (`Approvals`, `Workflow`, `Capsules`, `SyncQueue`, etc.) have no App-level guard; their own concurrency guarantees live in their packages (not audited here). No `sync.Once` fields — memoization is plain mutex + nil-check.\n\n**Dolt shared sql-server** — `internal/knowledge/dolt.go`:\n- `serverRegistry` (51-54): a process-global `map[string]*sharedServer` (keyed by cleaned data dir) with a refcount, guarded by its own mutex.\n- Cross-open sharing: `Open` (95-166) first tries `connectExistingServer` reading `.dolt/sql-server.info` (116, 172-186) to reuse a server started by *any* OS process; a same-process reuse joins the refcount via `joinInProcessServer` (65-73, `newReusedStore` 85-91). A freshly started server is recorded via `registerStartedServer` (77-81, 159).\n- `Close` (408-446) decrements the refcount; only the last in-process holder stops the process (415-419), and even then only if `otherClientsConnected()` (437,