eng/`cross_repository_impact`: `record_impact_edge`.\n- Semar/`change_dossier`: `create_change_dossier`, `add_dossier_claim`, `add_dossier_evidence`, `finalize_dossier`.\n- Semar/`handoff_capsule`: `create_handoff_capsule`.\n- Ungated (reads / store-enforced): `list_contradictions`, `analyze_impact`, `export_dossier`, `get`/`validate`/`resume` handoff, and `verify`/`dispute_dossier_claim` (these are inherently cross-role; the store's `ErrSelfVerification` rule enforces independence, surfaced as a clear MCP error).\n\n### Key behaviors wired\n- Dedup: `submit_contradiction` uses `contradiction.FindCandidates` and returns the existing record (`deduplicated=true`) on a normalized subject-key match, else `Put`s a new `detected` record with `Blocking = DefaultBlocking(severity)`.\n- `finalize_dossier` surfaces `*dossier.BlockingError`'s blocker list in the error message; `verify`/`dispute` surface `ErrSelfVerification`.\n- `resume_from_handoff` returns `handoff.ResumeContext` (smallest verified context) for resumable/refresh_required and errors on superseded/blocked/invalid.\n\n### Handoff ValidationDeps — wired vs TODO\n- **Wired:** `RoleConfigRevision` (roleconfig.Load .Revision), `ContradictionsChanged` (contradiction store; changed = left the open set or gone), `DossierSuperseded` (dossier store status), `PlanVersionExists` (lazy knowledge-store lookup — there is no dedicated plan store, so plans-of-record are knowledge records; a `// TODO` notes the integer version isn't verifiable there yet).\n- **Left nil (`// TODO`, nil=passing per the store contract):** `TaskIsCurrent`, `RepositoryStateMatches`, `EvidenceExists`.\n\n### Verification\n`go build ./...`, `go vet ./internal/mcpserver/...`, `gofmt -l internal/mcpserver` (prints nothing), and `go test ./internal/mcpserver/...` all green. Only `internal/mcpserver/` was touched.\n\nOne schema note worth flagging: because the MCP SDK infers input/output schemas from Go types, I introduced small `DossierClaimInput`/`DossierEvidenceInput` wrapper types (instead of embedding the protocol structs) to keep `id`/`status` optional at the tool boundary, and an `AnalyzeImpactOutput` wrapper with `omitempty` slices so an empty impact set serializes as omitted rather than a null array.</result>\n<usage><subagent_tokens>191080</subagent_tokens><tool_uses>60</tool_uses><duration_ms>911485</duration_ms></usage>\n</task-notification>",
