.Time` (required) :5918, `Section *string` :5921, `Uri *string` :5924, `Version interface{}` :5927.\n\n### Extraction (provenance) — `type KnowledgeRecordExtraction struct` :4767:\n`Confidence *float64` (0–1) :4768, `ExtractorVersion *string` :4771, `Method KnowledgeRecordExtractionMethod` (required) :4774. Method enum :4780: `model-assisted`, `manual`, `imported`.\n\n### Relations — `type KnowledgeRecordRelationsElem struct` :4980: `Target string` :4982, `Type KnowledgeRecordRelationsElemType` :4985. 22 relation-type consts :4990-5011 (`supersedes`, `derived-from`, `depends-on`, `related-to`, `conflicts-with`, `retrieves`, etc.).\n\n### Store — `internal/knowledge/dolt.go`\n- `type Store struct` :27 (holds `db *sql.DB`, `server *tools.BackgroundProcess`, event log path). Dolt over MySQL wire protocol.\n- `func Open(sup *tools.Supervisor, dataDir string) (*Store, error)` :103 — this is what `app.OpenKnowledge()` calls (rooted at `&lt;workspace&gt;/.punakawan/knowledge`).\n- `func (s *Store) DB() *sql.DB` :97 — exposed so taskstore shares the connection.\n- Schema `migrate()` :275: table `knowledge_records(id, type, status, validity_state, data JSON, updated_at)` plus `knowledge_relations(from_id, type, to_id)`.\n\n### Read/write methods (all `func (s *Store) …`)\n- `Get(id string) (protocol.KnowledgeRecord, error)` — `service.go:97`. Returns `ErrNotFound` (`service.go:14`) on miss.\n- `ListByType(recordType protocol.KnowledgeRecordType) ([]protocol.KnowledgeRecord, error)` — `service.go:114`.\n- `Related(id string) ([]protocol.KnowledgeRecord, error)` — `service.go:183` (reverse relation lookup).\n- `ListRecords(ctx, q KnowledgeListQuery) (records, nextCursor string, err error)` — `query.go:56`; `KnowledgeListQuery` struct `query.go:34` (fields `Type, Status, ValidityState, Repository, Source, Limit, Cursor`; keyset pagination).\n- `Count(ctx) (int, error)` — `query.go:18`.\n- `Put(rec) error` — `service.go:19` (upsert + relation reindex + event; retries transient Dolt 1213 conflicts).\n- `Supersede(id, supersededBy string) error` — `service.go:76` (sets `SupersededBy` + `validity.state=superseded`).\n- `Delete(id) error` — `service.go:141`.\n- `CheckStale(id, currentHash string) (bool, error)` — `staleness.go:36`.\n- **There is NO batch/GetMany.** Callers loop `Get` per id (e.g. `capsule.resolveRefs`, `search.finalize`).\n\n## 2. Search — `internal/search/search.go`\n\nEntry point: `func Search(store *knowledge.Store, ix *Index, req Request) ([]Result, error)` :113.\n\n- `type Request struct` :33: `Query string`, `Scope Scope`, `Types []string`, `Tags []string`, `IncludeRelated bool`, `Limit int`. Types/Tags are **hard filters** (`applyFilters` :386); Scope is ranking-only.\n- `type Scope struct` :25: `Project, Repository, Module, Path` (all `string`).\n- `type Result struct` :61: `Id, Title, Summary, Type string`, `Score float64`, `Match Match`, `Explanation []string`, `Record protocol.KnowledgeRecord` (fully hydrated only for surviving hits, `finalize` :579).\n- `type Match struct` :54: `Kind MatchKind`, `Fields []string`, `Terms []string`. `MatchKind` consts :45: `identifier, alias, bm25, fuzzy, related`.\n- **Match explanation field = `Result.Explanation []string`** (e.g. `\"Exact identifier: …\"`, `\"Same module: …\"`, `\"Verified\"`, `\"Type: …\"`, `\"Directly related to &lt;id&gt;\"`), built in `scoreResult` :414 / `expandRelations` :499.\n- Scope biases ranking via additive bonuses (`scoreResult` :432): `samePath=20`, `sameModule=12`, `sameRepository=8`, `sameProject=5` (mutually exclusive switch, most-specific wins); plus `exactIdentifier=100`, `exactAlias=40`, `directlyRelated=8`, `verifiedTrust=5` (const block :77-98). Pipeline: BM25F (`buildBM25FQuery` :325) ∪ identifier term query, fuzzy fallback only if empty, then one-hop relation expansion when `IncludeRelated`.\n- App wrapper: `func (a *App) SearchKnowledge(store, ix, req) ([]search.Result, error)` `app/app.go:351` — rebuilds index under lock then calls `Search`.\n\n## 3. Project selector — `internal/project/selector.go`\n\n- `PrioritySelector{Limit int}` :27; `func (s PrioritySelector) Select(p Project, capability, intent string, requestedKeys []string) []MetadataEntry` :32. Returns bounded `[]MetadataEntry` (default limit `DefaultSelectionLimit=8`, :8), deduped, in priority order: (1) requestedKeys in request order; (2) capability namespace (`key==capability` or prefix `\"&lt;capability&gt;.\"`); (3) exact intent match; (4) general fill in stored order — truncated to limit.\n- `type MetadataEntry struct` `project.go:46`: `Key string`, `Description string`, `Value any` (json+yaml tags).\n- `type Project struct` `project.go:56`: `ID, Name, Description string`, `Path string` (`yaml:\"-\"`, runtime-only), `Revision int`, `Metadata []MetadataEntry`.\n- `func (p *Project) MetadataFor(key string) (MetadataEntry, bool)` :381 (case-insensitive). `Revision` is optimistic-lock version bumped by Add/Update/DeleteMetadata; persisted via `Save` (`project.go:172`), loaded via `Load` (`project.go:90`, synthesizes zero-metadata project if no file).\n\n## 4. Recipe — `internal/recipe`\n\nTwo distinct types. The **retrieval-recipe** store is `Repository`/`Resolver`; `RecipeStore` (`store.go:55`) is a separate artifact-versioning adapter (walks SupersededBy chain for the artifact-review HTTP layer — tangential).\n\n- `type Repository struct { Store *knowledge.Store }` `repository.go:121`. Recipes are just `KnowledgeRecord`s of type `retrieval-recipe` with `RetrievalRecipe` populated — no separate persistence.\n  - `func (r *Repository) Search(q Query) ([]protocol.KnowledgeRecord, error)` :138 — structural filter (capability/provider/resource/operation/workspace-scope), restricted to `autoReusableStates` (`verified`, `stale` only; :110).\n  - `func (r *Repository) CreateVersion(rec, previousID string) (…, error)` :198 (Put + Supersede previous).\n  - `func (r *Repository) MarkState(recipeID, state, reason) error` :222.\n  - `type Query struct` :93: `Capability, Provider, Resource, Operation, WorkspaceID, RepositoryID`.\n- `type Resolver struct { Repo *Repository }` `resolver.go:92`.\n  - `func (r *Resolver) Resolve(req OperationRequest) (Resolution, error)` :97 — scores/ranks (weights :69-89), returns `Resolution{Outcome, Selected *Candidate, Candidates []Candidate}` :49. `Outcome` :22: `resolved, stale, ambiguous, not_found`.\n  - `type OperationRequest struct` :13: `Capability, Intent, WorkspaceID string`, `RepositoryIDs []string` — describes **what the task needs (capability+intent)**, which is the lookup key.\n- Recipe execution — `internal/recipe/operation.go`: `type Executor struct` :51; `func (e *Executor) ResolveAndExecute(ctx, req OperationRequest, bindings map[string]any, runID, taskID string, now) (*ExecutionResult, error)` :84. It compiles the recipe selector into a provider query (JQL) and runs it against a live provider (`JiraSearchClient`), records evidence — **it produces `ExecutionResult{RecipeID, RecipeVersion, CompiledQuery, Issues []ResultRow, Evidence protocol.EvidenceRecord}`** (:75). It does **not** produce knowledge ids or a `search.Request`; it is a live external-data fetch, distinct from `internal/search`.\n- Recipe body — `type KnowledgeRecordRetrievalRecipe struct` `protocol:5088`: `Capability`, `Intent`, `Provider`, `Resource`, `Operation`, `ReadOnly bool`, `RecipeVersion *int`, `Selector` (AST, :5138), `Inputs`, `Ordering`, `Output` (:5312 EntityType/Fields/IdentityField), `AppliesTo *…{WorkspaceIds, RepositoryIds}` (:5146), `Validation *…`, `LastExecution *…` (:5192, mutable \"latest execution\" summary; status enum success/failure :5223).\n\n## 5. Capsule building &amp; the title-only-summary problem — `internal/capsule`\n\n- `Build(store *knowledge.Store, id string, now time.Time, in BuildInput) (protocol.ContextCapsule, error)` `build.go:67`. `type BuildInput struct` :13 (`TaskID, Role, Objective, RequirementIDs, KnowledgeIDs, EvidenceIDs, KnowledgeReasons map[string]string, AcceptanceCriteria, Constraints, …, ProjectMetadata`).\n- **THE BUG / title-only reduction — `build.go:178-183`:**\n  ```go\n  func summaryPtr(r protocol.KnowledgeRecord) *string {\n      if r.Title == \"\" { return nil }\n      return &amp;r.Title\n  }\n  ```\n  Called by `toRequirementRefs` (`build.go:158`) and `toKnowledgeRefs` (`build.go:169`) — every resolved record is reduced to **only its `Title`** as the capsule item's `Summary`. `r.Summary` and `r.Content` and the type-specific payloads are ignored.\n- Capsule item structs (in `protocol`): `ContextCapsuleRequirementsElem{Id string; Summary *string}` :2441; `ContextCapsuleRelevantKnowledgeElem{Id string; Reason *string; Summary *string}` :2409; `ContextCapsuleEvidenceElem{Id string; Summary *string}` :2347.\n- `ContextCapsule` struct :2280 fields: `Id, TaskId, CreatedAt, Digest, Role, Objective, Requirements[], AcceptanceCriteria[], Constraints[], RelevantKnowledge[], Evidence[], Assumptions[], UnresolvedQuestions[], AllowedTools[] (required), ForbiddenActions[] (required), ExpectedOutput *string, TokenBudget *int, ProjectMetadata[], RoleGuidance *string`. `Role` enum :2467: `gareng, petruk, bagong`.\n- Retrieval path: `BuildFromRetrieval(ctx, store, ix, id, now, in RetrievalInput) (…)` `retrieve.go:89` — runs `search.Search`, greedily selects within `TokenBudget` (cost = `estimateTokens(Title)+estimateTokens(Summary)`, `retrieve.go:128` — again only title+summary), records `search.Result.Explanation` as each item's `reason`. `estimateTokens` = ~len/4 (`retrieve.go:35`).\n- Record types &amp; bounded summaries: each record type carries distinct rich content — free-text records use `Summary`/`Content`; structured role outputs use their payload struct (e.g. `SemarSynthesis` :5843 has `Goal, KnownFacts[], Risks[], OpenQuestions[]`; `FinalPlan` :4835 has `AcceptanceCriteria[], ArchitectureDecision`, etc.); recipes use `RetrievalRecipe`. A per-type bounded summarizer would read these instead of falling back to `Title`.\n- Forbidden-type-per-role policy (leakage guard): `internal/capsule/policy.go` — `ForbiddenKnowledgeTypes(role)` :15, `IsForbiddenKnowledgeType` :41, `ForbiddenTools` :53 (bagong blocked from `write_file, bulk_create_files, commit_task`).\n- Capsule persistence: `internal/capsule/store.go` — `Store` is append-only JSONL at `.punakawan/capsules/capsules.jsonl`; `OpenStore(workspaceRoot)` :26, `Put` :40, `Get(id)` :97, `List()` :63. `ErrNotFound` :57. Not the Dolt store.\n\n## 6. How MCP tools reach the stores — `internal/mcpserver`\n\nHandler shape (go-sdk): a handler constructor takes `*app.App` and returns\n`func(ctx context.Context, req *mcp.CallToolRequest, in &lt;Input&gt;) (*mcp.CallToolResult, &lt;Output&gt;, error)`. The returned `&lt;Output&gt;` struct is the tool's **StructuredContent** (returned as the 2nd value; `*mcp.CallToolResult` is returned `nil`). Registration: `addTool(server, reg, &amp;mcp.Tool{Name, Description}, handler(a))` — `tools.go:36-44` (request_capsule at :41-44), :270 (search_knowledge); `addTool` wraps `mcp.AddTool` (`tools.go:17`).\n\n- **searchKnowledgeHandler** — `tools_knowledgesearch.go:58`. Gets stores via `a.OpenKnowledge()` (:60) and `a.OpenSearchIndex()` (:64), calls `a.SearchKnowledge(store, ix, search.Request{…})` (:75). Input `SearchKnowledgeInput` :18 (`Query`, `Project/Repository/Module/Path`, `Types[], Tags[], IncludeRelated bool, Limit int` — json+jsonschema tags). Output `SearchKnowledgeOutput{Results []SearchKnowledgeResult}` :54; `SearchKnowledgeResult` :42 (`Id, Title, Summary, Type, Score`, `Match SearchKnowledgeMatch`, `Explanation []string`).\n- **requestCapsuleHandler** — `tools_capsule.go:61`. `store, _ := a.OpenKnowledge()` (:68), optionally `a.OpenSearchIndex()`+`search.Rebuild` (:104-110), calls `capsule.Build` / `capsule.BuildFromRetrieval`, then `a.Capsules.Put(c)` (:149). Input `RequestCapsuleInput` :18; output is `protocol.ContextCapsule` directly. Project metadata folded via `selectProjectMetadata(a.Workspace.Root, capability, intent, keys)` (:77) → `toCapsuleMetadata` (:97).\n- `a.OpenTaskStore()` (`app/app.go:277`) opens the Beads-less fallback task store, sharing knowledge's Dolt connection (`taskstore.New(k.DB())`).\n- Input/output struct conventions: plain Go structs with `json:\"snake_case,omitempty\"` tags; user-facing tools add `jsonschema:\"…description…\"` tags for LLM guidance (e.g. `tools_capsule.go:20-58`, `tools_knowledgesearch.go:29-30`). `build_task_context` (`tools_taskcontext.go`) embeds a domain struct: `BuildTaskContextOutput{ taskcontext.Context; ProjectMetadata []MetadataContextEntry }` (:48).\n- Metadata render precedent (bounded per-entry text block): `MetadataContextEntry{Key, Description, Value any, Rendered string}` `metadata_context.go:22`; `renderMetadataEntry` :113 produces the `key\\n  description\\n  Value: &lt;v&gt;` block.\n\n## 7. Digest / hashing precedent\n\nTwo existing canonical-hash helpers, both `\"sha256:&lt;hex&gt;\"` schema-compliant (`^sha256:[0-9a-f]{64}$`):\n- **`capsule.Digest(c protocol.ContextCapsule) (string, error)`** — `internal/capsule/capsule.go:46`. Hashes a fixed-order `digestPayload` (`capsule.go:28`) of the substantive fields only (role, objective, requirements, acceptance_criteria, constraints, relevant_knowledge, evidence, allowed_tools, forbidden_actions — excludes id/digest/task_id/created_at/token_budget/assumptions/unresolved_questions/project_metadata/role_guidance). Relies on struct-field declaration order for stable bytes; `nonNil` (:70) normalizes nil vs empty slices. Verified in `requireCapsuleForRole` (`tools_capsule.go:172`).\n- **`knowledge.ContentHash(data []byte) string`** — `internal/knowledge/staleness.go:17`. Plain `sha256` of arbitrary bytes; used for source content_hash / staleness comparison (`CheckStale` :36).\n- Ad-hoc precedent: recipe execution hashes compiled JQL with `sha256` → `\"sha256:\"+hex` inline (`internal/recipe/operation.go:258-259`).</result>\n<usage>